  "result": "The rule for NRS_484B_153_3 passed the gate (**OK**) on the first run, using 1 of the 6 runs. `task_result.md` is written.\n\nOne slip: before the first gate run, I made one shell call that was not the exact gate command (the same command with `--help` added). The permission check denied it and it never ran, so it used none of the budget. I noted this in `task_result.md`.\n\n**The rule** (`NRS_484B_153_3.lean`):\n- **Who it covers:** the vehicle is a member of `DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle`.\n- **When it applies:** the vehicle's door on the traffic side is open (`sig_door_open(subject, traffic)`).\n- **What it requires:** that door has not been open at every observation over the last `p.traffic_side_door_max_open` seconds (60 s in this run).\n\nI made no choices beyond what the node states, so I declared no narrowings.\n\n**The witnesses** are all a car stopped at the curb, sampled once a second:\n\n| Witness | What happens | Expected |\n|---|---|---|\n| forbid | traffic-side door open for 300 s, judged from 61 s on | violated |\n| permit | traffic-side door open only from 80 to 94 s (15 s) | compliant |\n| idle | only the curb-side door is open | not applicable |\n| blind | door state masked | unknown |\n\nThe forbid and permit judging windows start at 61 s, so no judged moment has a 60-second look-back that reaches past the start of the trace.",
